critic.designVerdict:
REVISION REQUIRED, consolidated for disposition C. This is local and read-only; NOTHING was run, and a favourable design review is not source permission.

The protocol core is COMPATIBLE AS DESIGN with doc 49's 5C, the 462cf79 correction, doc 51 and its 24 carry-forwards (7b1e606, 81a32af), Samuel's 1d4f2c3 scope, currentness at S 25858ad and the accepted 3e82154. That core:
- actor/key lock, then replay before mutable gates;
- preflight row locks, then the head last;
- AFTER-statement guards with a scoped epoch;
- a single-owner definer commit;
- five atomic writes, with no legacy submit;
- persisted:true only after commit;
- read_all readback;
- declarations only, never paid/fulfilled/reserved.

Five P2s block drafting the bodies or writing an exact grant:
- C-1: the authority read and activation source are unnamed, and the reader at S is constant 'unavailable', so no save can succeed.
- C-2: the guard's definer/owner model is missing, and its absent-head rule fails open.
- C-3: FOR SHARE locks on the single head row can starve publish/revoke/guard FOR UPDATE, so first-lock-wins revocation has no bounded wait.
- C-4: payment-bearing paths are included with no need.
- C-5: the commit's host file and gate are unnamed.

How the lens disagreements were resolved:
- C1-F3 drops to P3 (disclosed gap, overstated wording).
- C1-F10 is refuted; QO catalogVersion is the static bindings path.
- C2-F1 and C2-F2 drop to P3.
- C2-F7 resolves to: the QO port private context is mandatory for any non-synthetic save; the express.ts seam is the next named item.
- The lens grant's contradiction (authorise the activation source, exclude activation) resolves as: authored only, never invoked.

Added by this critic: C-26 (transition-table trigger mechanics).

